bash      5.3.15(1)-release
started   2026-09-23T08:25:18Z

cited document declares: revision 3

LIVE   the committed state of the two documents
  live    : cites revision 3, cited document declares revision 3 -> MATCH

MUTANT the citation is rolled back one revision (the r8 defect, restored)
  mutant  : cites revision 2, cited document declares revision 3 -> STALE

INERT  a wording change at the same site, the revision left alone
  inert   : cites revision 3, cited document declares revision 3 -> MATCH

RESULT: live MATCH, mutant STALE (red), inert MATCH (green). The check
        reds on the edit that actually happens -- a revision moving
        under a citation -- and not on a reword beside it.
